commit f7f5dc45e51c56f20b4796b77b58d6e257c5fc29
Author: Liz <liz@gewelf.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 22:56:09 2026 -0400

    perf(read): zero-copy byte arrays on flat reads

    BYTE_ARRAY values decoded from PLAIN and dictionary pages (V1 and V2) are
    now slices of the page buffer or dictionary page instead of per-value
    copies. readColumnDynamicWithData enables this (column_decoder.borrow_bytes)
    only when it owns the page buffers and value_mod.bytes_arena_allocator is
    set: it then allocates the uncompressed chunk, or each decompressed page,
    from that arena and never frees them, and builds the string dictionary with
    StringDictionary.fromPlainBorrowed. Borrowed bytes therefore live exactly
    as long as the arena copies did: until the streaming iterator's per-row-group
    reset, or the reader's bytes arena deinit for readAllRows/rowIterator.
    Value.deinit already skips bytes in that scope and rows are bytes_borrowed.
    Filtered reads (caller-owned page data), FLBA, decimals, delta encodings,
    arrow_batch and the typed decoder keep copying.

    Also re-exports StreamingRowIterator from lib.zig.

    make bench (0.16, ReleaseFast), best of 6 alternating runs, rows/s:
                      read_stream          read                 write
      int64_plain     151.3M -> 148.0M     45.4M -> 44.9M       56.9M -> 55.9M
      f64_plain       151.0M -> 148.5M     45.2M -> 44.6M       56.3M -> 55.8M
      int64_nullable  132.7M -> 134.4M     43.5M -> 43.5M       75.9M -> 75.0M
      str_dict         49.8M ->  79.9M     28.0M -> 35.9M       18.4M -> 18.3M
      str_unique       46.3M ->  70.0M     26.9M -> 33.8M       13.3M -> 13.2M
      mixed5           21.1M ->  25.2M     10.5M -> 11.5M        4.9M ->  4.9M
    file_MB unchanged for every scenario.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M67Y5N7T1GPNJYRMW4X8TS62

